## Context

The manuscript's §5 "Fifth, a tailored solution can work"
(`slides/manuscript/main.md` lines 56–62) describes a stateful
agentic workflow: a knowledge base of narrative asset histories,
fully sourced; the statistical table is a derived artefact of the
narrative inventory; initial generation by deep-research heroic
prompt; automatic verification of the four §2 quality dimensions;
incremental update with new documents; memory of human judgements
preserved.

Unlike Exp 1 and Exp 2, this is closer to a **demonstration / case
study** than a clean N-rep sweep — the value is the integrated
workflow producing one carefully audited inventory, not a
distribution of F1 scores. This ticket pins the spec and runs the
demonstration.

Replaces the §5 portion of the now-closed 0153.

## Relevant files

- `slides/manuscript/main.md` lines 56–62 — §5 prose to
  operationalise.
- `slides/manuscript/main.md` Annex A — pattern to adapt (a case
  study annex will differ from a sweep annex; both are valid).
- `experiments/` — likely needs a sub-directory for stateful
  workflow artefacts (narrative store, source links, judgement log).
- `src/aedist/` — current modules assume one-shot prompt → table;
  stateful workflow needs new orchestration.
- 0146 (capability-timeline-expand-and-figure) — may overlap on the
  "incremental update" angle.

## Actions

1. **Pin the workflow architecture.** Define the components:
   narrative store schema (per-asset, per-cell provenance),
   initial-extraction agent (deep-research-style), four
   automatic-verifier agents (one per quality dimension), update
   orchestrator, human-judgement memory. Decide which already exist
   in the codebase vs. need building.
2. **Pin the demonstration scope.** Vietnam thermal fleet (same as
   Exp 1) — start from the deep-research output of Exp 2's best
   agent, run through the workflow, produce the final reconciled
   inventory. One run, not a sweep.
3. **Define success criteria.** Row-level F1 vs Exp 1 ceiling; cell-
   level provenance resolve rate; temporal validity per cell;
   coherence (internal consistency). Decide what "acceptable
   scientific quality" means as a numeric threshold for §5's claim
   to be supported.
4. **Annex D in `main.md`.** Author the workflow spec. Will differ
   from Annex A — this is a system architecture, not a sweep matrix.
5. **Build the missing components.** Each verifier and the
   orchestration loop, with tests.
6. **Run the demonstration.** One full pass on the Vietnam fleet.
   Capture the audit trail (per-cell provenance, per-judgement
   record, time-and-cost summary).
7. **Update H-verdicts.** §5 primarily tests H3 (Accuracy–provenance
   joint optimisation) — does the stateful workflow break the
   incompatibility observed in Exp 1 / Exp 2? Also touches H4
   (local-model viability) if the workflow is re-run with a local
   backbone.
8. **Update manuscript prose.** Replace §5's forward-looking "we aim
   to demonstrate" with the observed outcome.

## Test

- `tests/test_narrative_store_schema.py` — round-trip on a small
  fixture; per-cell (source, date, confidence, conflict-resolution)
  tuple preserved.
- `tests/test_verifier_*.py` — one per quality dimension; happy-path
  + at-least-one-failure-mode fixture.
- `tests/test_annex_d_present.py` — adherence: main.md has Annex D
  describing the workflow.

## Invariants

- The narrative is the source of truth; the table is derived.
  Adding a row to the table without a corresponding narrative entry
  must fail.
- Every cell carries provenance — no anonymous values.
- Human-judgement memory is append-only — corrections create new
  entries, never overwrite.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Annex D in `main.md` describes the workflow architecture and
      the demonstration scope.
- [ ] Narrative store + four verifiers + orchestrator implemented
      and tested.
- [ ] One demonstration run on Vietnam fleet completed; audit trail
      captured.
- [ ] H3 (and H4 if local-backbone run is included) updated in
      `docs/hypotheses.md`.
- [ ] §5 manuscript prose updated with observed outcome.
- [ ] `make report.pdf` and `make slides.pdf` rebuild cleanly.
